<title>USA: JW Charles Q4 shr $0.56 vs $0.23.</title>
<headline>JW Charles Q4 shr $0.56 vs $0.23.</headline>
<dateline>BOCA RATON, Fla. 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In millions, except per share data)</p>
<p>				  Quarter Ended	 Year Ended</p>
<p>				December 31,	December 31,</p>
<p>			   1996	  1995    1966	1995</p>
<p>Revenues	   $   23.1    $   21.7 $  91.0   $  80.0</p>
<p>Net Income	    2.021	 1.388     6.0	 3.8</p>
<p>Earnings per</p>
<p> common share	  0.56	  0.23    1.27	0.63</p>
<p>NOTES: Full company name is JWCharles Financial Services Inc.</p>
<p>In June 1996, the repurchase of Gilman CMG Inc's 49 percent interest in the company was completed. On a proforma basis, assuming that the repurchase had been effected on January 1, 1996, JWCharles would have reported earnings per common share of $1.62 against the $1.27 actually reported for the 12-months ended December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>--((New York Newsdesk, 212-859-1610))</p>
